yes, write yourself a `retrieve situtation macro' which inserts enough
vertical space to get back onto a multiple of the baselineskip. call
it frequently, like after sections. I append some code I started to
write, with advice from Phil Taylor and Chris Rowley, but I got
depressed and stopped. so all you gurus dont laugh, OK?

\newdimen\desired
\newcount\xlines
\def\resynch{
\xlines=0\desired=\topskip
\loop\advance\xlines by 1\advance\desired by \baselineskip
\ifnum \desired < \pagetotal\repeat
\advance\desired by -\pagetotal
\typeout{\the\pagetotal-----> \the\desired}
\vskip\desired}

